# M4 — the `DISCARD ALL` block deleted from finishScopedTransaction.
#
# Canon 7.6 names pooled-identity leak across two sequential requests on one warmed
# client a RELEASE BLOCKER. DISCARD ALL always worked: on a reused backend (same
# pg_backend_pid) it clears a planted session-level GUC and a prepared statement. It had
# no control, so the release blocker was unguarded by the suite.
#
# Removing the block also removes the `tainted` write that a FAILING DISCARD ALL performs,
# so a connection whose state could not be cleared is returned to the pool instead of
# being destroyed (V5: a set_config with is_local=false survives the COMMIT).
#
# The named catcher asserts the same-backend condition explicitly — without it, two calls
# landing on two different pooled connections would pass whether or not anything was
# discarded.
id: M4
title: the `DISCARD ALL` block deleted from finishScopedTransaction
expect: caught
proves: canon 7.6's pooled-identity-leak release blocker is controlled, on one proven-reused backend
expect-test: a session GUC and a prepared statement planted in call 1 are GONE in call 2 on the SAME backend

file: src/server/db/scoped.ts
count: 1
@@FIND
  try {
    await client.query('discard all')
  } catch {
    tainted = true
  }
  client.release(tainted ? true : undefined)
@@REPLACE
  client.release(tainted ? true : undefined)
@@END
